# The head of the loop goes by the length of the list, and each turn takes an element off.
# The lie, testing=StorageAndLengthsAreTakenToBeAsInFront: the turns of a loop are taken to leave the storage of lists and of views, and so their lengths, as they were in front of it: what a turn reads of them is read once, in front. The loop has as many turns as the list was long. No turn reads an element.
# Under testing=TestsEveryPosition (--aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges) and testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime (--aot-harden=proof-checks) the same records are built at the same places, and what was read in front is held against the cell in the turn: the process stops by name.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# RIGHT: 4 4
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: 4 4
# HELD-NEXT: exited with 0
# The lie as built: another answer, and nobody stops.
# RUN(SILENT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=StorageAndLengthsAreTakenToBeAsInFront
# SILENT: 8 0
# SILENT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(POSITIONS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=TestsEveryPosition,StorageAndLengthsAreTakenToBeAsInFront
